---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const mug=core.products.find(p=>p.product_id==='P7');
---
<figure class="routing" aria-labelledby="r26-routing-title">
 <figcaption id="r26-routing-title"><span>Figure 1</span> The shop key decides where the request goes</figcaption>
 <shop-route>
  <div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Request to route"><button data-query="receipt" aria-pressed="true">Shop 10’s order 103</button><button data-query="mug" aria-pressed="false">P7 without a shop</button><button data-query="catalogue" aria-pressed="false">Both shops’ products</button></div>
  <p class="request" data-request>Request carries shop_id = 10 → shard A</p>
  <div class="shards">
   <section data-shard="a" class="selected"><p class="panel-title">Shard A · shop 10</p><p class="route-label" data-route-a>↓ read here</p><div class="rows"><p>products: (10, {mug.product_id}) · {mug.name} · {mug.price}</p><p>orders: (10, 103) · Mina · pending</p><p>order_items: (10, 103, 1) · P7 × 1 at 20.00</p><p>order_items: (10, 103, 2) · P3 × 2 at 4.50</p></div></section>
   <section data-shard="b"><p class="panel-title">Shard B · shop 20</p><p class="route-label" data-route-b>Not contacted</p><div class="rows"><p>products: (20, P7) · Copper mug · 18.00</p><p class="scope">Other shop 20 rows are outside this drawing.</p></div></section>
  </div>
  <p class="result" data-result aria-live="polite">The receipt’s order, lines and products are all on shard A. Shop 20’s P7 cannot join to shop 10’s line.</p>
 </shop-route>
 <p class="caption">A chosen tenant-placement model, with selected rows from the tenant-scoped schema. Every related table is deliberately placed by shop_id, and a router knows each shop’s owner. Real engines need corresponding distribution and co-location configuration; primary-key syntax alone does not produce these boxes. Replicas and individual storage ranges are omitted.</p>
 <details><summary>Routing in words</summary><p>A request scoped to shop 10 reaches A. P7 without a shop could mean either mug, so this scheme must ask A and B. A list across both shops also asks both and combines their results.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 class ShopRoute extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback(){
   if(this.dataset.ready)return;this.dataset.ready='true';
   const cases={receipt:['Request carries shop_id = 10 → shard A','The receipt’s order, lines and products are all on shard A. Shop 20’s P7 cannot join to shop 10’s line.'],mug:['Request carries product_id = P7, with no shop → shards A and B','Two different products match: (10, P7), Blue mug at 20.00; (20, P7), Copper mug at 18.00. P7 alone is not a global identity.'],catalogue:['Request spans shop_id IN (10, 20) → shards A and B','Both shards contribute rows. The coordinator combines the results; a required global order or limit must apply to that combined answer.']};
   for(const button of this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-query]'))button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
    const key=button.dataset.query as keyof typeof cases;const both=key!=='receipt';
    for(const b of this.querySelectorAll('button'))b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button));
    this.querySelector('[data-request]')!.textContent=cases[key][0];this.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=cases[key][1];
    this.querySelector('[data-shard=b]')!.classList.toggle('selected',both);this.querySelector('[data-route-b]')!.textContent=both?'↓ read here':'Not contacted';
   });
  }
 }
 if(!customElements.get('shop-route'))customElements.define('shop-route',ShopRoute);
</script>
<style>
.routing{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem}shop-route{display:block;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:1rem}.choices{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem}.choices button{font:.85rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer}.choices button[aria-pressed=true]{border:2px solid var(--color-accent);font-weight:700}.choices button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}.request{font:.95rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);padding:.8rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.shards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem}.shards section{margin:0;border:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.shards section.selected{border:2px solid var(--color-accent)}.panel-title{font:600 .95rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);margin:0}.route-label{font:.8rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);min-height:1.5rem}.rows p{font:.82rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);border-top:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.5rem 0;margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.rows .scope{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.result{font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.5rem .8rem;min-height:4.5rem}.caption,details{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:550px){.shards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.choices button{width:100%}.result{min-height:0}}
</style>
